lue of ${\\int }_{-4}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" "![](images/11/11cf2a28b6ce6281de0299a4a585bc3c98bf891f6d958401f22aab2fc6ce5ef2.png)\n\nGiven the graph of $y=f(x)$ above, find the value of $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{-4}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186332678 :question/problem "![](images/e0/e0fc07ac8466381b668877e25cd0c9d8d5258a9061548e7b8efb12f75f6a0f04.png)\n\nThe graph of a function $y=f(x)$ is shown above. It consists of two lines and the arc of a quarter-circle of radius $2.$ Given $g(t)={\\int }_{-2}^{t}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x,$ determine the value of $g(3).$" "![](images/e0/e0fc07ac8466381b668877e25cd0c9d8d5258a9061548e7b8efb12f75f6a0f04.png)\n\nThe graph of a function $y=f(x)$ is shown above. It consists of two lines and the arc of a quarter-circle of radius $2.$ Given $$\n\\displaystyle g(t)={\\int }_{-2}^{t}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$ determine the value of $g(3).$"] [:db/cas 17592186332679 :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{-4}^{-1}\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "Evaluate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{-4}^{-1}\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186332680 :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{-2}^{-1}\\frac{1}{{x}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "Evaluate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{-2}^{-1}\\frac{1}{{x}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186332681 :question/problem "Find the function $f(x)$ and the value of $b,$ given that ${\\int }_{e}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(e+\\frac{ie}{n})\\cdot \\frac{e}{n}].$" "Find the function $f(x)$ and the value of $b,$ given that $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{e}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(e+\\frac{ie}{n})\\cdot \\frac{e}{n}].\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186332683 :question/problem "Given that ${\\int }_{0}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-5$ and ${\\int }_{4}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=8$ then what is ${\\int }_{0}^{7}(7+3f(x))\\,\\text{d}x?$" "Given that $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{0}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-5\n$$ and $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{4}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=8\n$$ then what is $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{0}^{7}(7+3f(x))\\,\\text{d}x?\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186332684 :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡3x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "Calculate $$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡3x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186332685 :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{\\pi /8}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{{sin}^{2}⁡(2x)}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "Evaluate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{\\pi /8}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{{sin}^{2}⁡(2x)}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186332686 :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{4}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "Calculate $$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{4}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186332686 :question/worked-solution "We use the identity $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{4}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "We use the identity $$\n\\displaystyle \\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\n$$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{4}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186332687 :question/problem "$\\int \\operatorname{cot}⁡x(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\operatorname{cot}⁡x(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186332687 :question/worked-solution "We multiply out the parentheses and then use the identities $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x},$ and $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{cot}⁡x(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-x+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "We multiply out the parentheses and then use the identities $$\n\\displaystyle \\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x},\n$$ and $$\n\\displaystyle \\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x},\n$$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{cot}⁡x(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-x+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186332688 :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "Calculate $$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186332688 :question/worked-solution "We use the identity $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "We use the identity $$\n\\displaystyle \\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x},\n$$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186332689 :question/problem "$\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x{sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=$" "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x{sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186332690 :question/problem "$\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡3x\\operatorname{sec}⁡3x\\,\\text{d}x=$" "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡3x\\operatorname{sec}⁡3x\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186332691 :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "Calculate $$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186332691 :question/worked-solution "We can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\operatorname{tan}⁡4x\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe then use the fact that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡4x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}$ to express this as\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the identity $\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}=\\operatorname{sec}⁡4x$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {sec}^{2}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this by substitution. Let $u=4x.$ Then $\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{4}\\text{d}u.$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {sec}^{2}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {sec}^{2}⁡u\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\int {sec}^{2}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{tan}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{tan}⁡4x+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "We can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\operatorname{tan}⁡4x\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe then use the fact that $$\n\\displaystyle \\operatorname{tan}⁡4x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}\n$$ to express this as\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the identity $\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}=\\operatorname{sec}⁡4x$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {sec}^{2}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this by substitution. Let $u=4x.$ Then $\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{4}\\text{d}u.$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {sec}^{2}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {sec}^{2}⁡u\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\int {sec}^{2}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{tan}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{tan}⁡4x+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186332692 :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{1}{{sec}^{2}⁡2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "Calculate $$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{1}{{sec}^{2}⁡2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186332693 :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "Evaluate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$"]]
